{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_three_forms","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.collatz_three_forms","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.no_nontrivial_periodic_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.no_nontrivial_periodic_trace","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L238-L258","doc":"**The categorical face implies categorical cycle-exclusion.** Under the\nconjecture, `𝒞_q` has no periodic orbit whose trace differs from the unknot\nvalue: a period-`p` orbit's trace sequence is periodic, and eventual\nconvergence to `1` then forces it to equal `1` outright.\n\nThis is the coupling C12 asks for. It is the categorical shadow of the arc's\narithmetic cycle-exclusion results (`qcollatz_no_adj_tail_cycle`,\n`qcollatz_no_front_loaded_cycle`), which exclude cycles on the Skein side by a\nheight obstruction — so the two faces are now related by a theorem rather than\nby prose. **Conditional**: it assumes the open conjecture and proves nothing\nabout it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.identity_unique_attractor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.identity_unique_attractor","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L236-L236","doc":"Uniqueness of the attractor: any fixed point already has unknot trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.trace_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.trace_converges","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L234-L234","doc":"The displayed convergence: every orbit's trace is eventually the unknot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L232-L232","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.MarkovTraceConvergence","kind":"class","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L221-L236","doc":"**`conj:q-collatz`, categorical face — a §3b-tax PRIMARY conjecture carrier.**\n\n`tr_M(𝒞_q^k(h)) → 1` for every `h ∈ H_n(q)`: every braid untangles to the\nunknot under iterated crossing resolution and destabilization, and the\nidentity braid is the *unique* attractor.\n\n**There is deliberately no instance.** The absence is the honest encoding of\nan open problem: per AGENTS.md, an axiom or a fabricated instance is not a\nproof, and supplying one here would be an audit dodge. Both fields carry real\ncontent — neither is `True` and the class is not an empty marker — so a\ndownstream `[MarkovTraceConvergence sys]` result is a genuine conditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.identity_orbit_trace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.identity_orbit_trace_one","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L213-L219","doc":"**The conjecture's target is attained** — unconditionally, no class needed.\nThe identity braid's whole orbit has trace `1`, so the conclusion of\n`MarkovTraceConvergence` is not vacuously unreachable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.identity_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.identity_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L209-L209","doc":"The step fixes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.trM_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.trM_identity","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L207-L207","doc":"Its trace is the unknot value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.identity","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L205-L205","doc":"The identity braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.step","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L203-L203","doc":"One application of the Skein-Collatz operator `𝒞_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.trM","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L201-L201","doc":"The Markov trace `tr_M : H_n(q) → 𝒮(q)`, sending braid words to Jones\npolynomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L198-L198","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.HeckeCollatzSystem","kind":"structure","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L191-L209","doc":"The categorical setup: a carrier `H` (the Hecke algebra `H_n(q)` in the\nintended reading) with a Markov trace into the Skein ring `S`, a Collatz step\noperator, and a distinguished identity braid whose trace is the unknot value\n`1` and which the step fixes.\n\nThis is **setup, not conjecture** — every field is a definitional property of\nthe identity braid, discharged in any intended model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.classical_limit_is_critical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.classical_limit_is_critical","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L176-L187","doc":"**The classical case has no margin.** The expected number of halvings per\ntripling at `q = 1` equals the integer threshold `2` established in\n`integer_threshold_eq_two` — the remark's *\"There is no margin.\"*\n\nStated as a conjunction of two facts about two different kinds of object (an\nexpectation and a sufficiency threshold), deliberately **not** as an\nequivalence between them: they are numerically equal, which is what \"critical\"\nmeans here, and nothing stronger is asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.expected_halvings_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.expected_halvings_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L166-L174","doc":"**`E[v₂(3n+1)] = ∑_{k} k·2^{-k} = 2`** — the remark's displayed identity,\nexactly. (The `n = 0` term contributes `0`, so summing over all of `ℕ` agrees\nwith the remark's sum from `k = 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.odd_branch_at_divisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.odd_branch_at_divisor","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L153-L158","doc":"**The odd branch degenerates to a shift at the divisor.** Since `[3]_q ↦ 1`,\nthe numerator `[3]_q·P + 1` of an odd step becomes `P + 1`. This is why the\ndomain condition of the Skein-Collatz map is `P|_{q=-1} ∈ {0, -1}`: those are\nexactly the values at which one more halving is available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi3_at_divisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi3_at_divisor","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L150-L151","doc":"**`[3]_q = 1` at the divisor** — the remark's `[3]_q|_{q=-1} = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi2_at_divisor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi2_at_divisor","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L147-L148","doc":"**`[2]_q` vanishes at the divisor.** `q = -1` is the `[2]_q`-divisor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L133-L139","doc":"**The contact threshold lies strictly between one and two halvings.** This is\nthe two-sided statement `QOU.Substrate.contact_threshold_lt_two` announces;\nits lower half is new here. Being strictly above `1` and strictly below `2`,\nthe least sufficient *integer* number of halvings is exactly `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L120-L131","doc":"`v* < 2`, restated self-containedly (the archimedean\n`QOU.Substrate.contact_threshold_lt_two` proves the same over `qInt`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.one_lt_contactThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.one_lt_contactThreshold","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L108-L118","doc":"**`1 < v*` — the half `QOU.Substrate.contact_threshold_lt_two` claims in its\ndocstring and does not prove.** Without it, `v = 1` is not ruled out and the\nremark's *\"the integer threshold is exactly 2\"* has no support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.contactThreshold","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L104-L106","doc":"The real contact threshold `v* = log [3]_q / log [2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.integer_threshold_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.integer_threshold_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L83-L97","doc":"**The integer contraction threshold is exactly `v = 2`**, for every `q > 0` —\nthe remark's *\"Two halvings per tripling are required\"*, with no\ntranscendental quantity involved. Three claims: `v = 1` never suffices,\n`v = 2` always does, and no `v` below `2` can suffice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi3_lt_qi2_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi3_lt_qi2_sq","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L77-L81","doc":"`[3]_q < [2]_q²`: two halvings always do. Their difference is exactly the\nsubstrate parameter `q` — the algebraic gap of\n`QOU.Substrate.qInt_gap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi2_lt_qi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.CollatzThreeForms.qi2_lt_qi3","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/collatz_three_forms.lean#L73-L75","doc":"`[2]_q < [3]_q`: one halving never pays for a tripling. Their difference is\n`q²`, so this is strict for every `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}